OWED: obligation transit — send must CONSUME the binding's custody into the vessel; `| some v` mints v: Src<live!> at the winning arm. TODAY (measured): send copies the value in plain; custody stays with the producer binding and auto-discharge fires `dispose(s)` at the producer's scope — so the consumer sees KORU030 'v holds no live obligation'. The current semantics are "copy-in, dispose-at-source": safe by accident for dead data, a poisoned-resource launderer for protos owning real handles (the ring copy's fd is dead the moment the producer discharges). Rung: send consumes <live!> on `ok` only; `| full` / `| closed` leave custody untouched; recv mints the obligation fresh per-delivery.
